      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "9#1",
      "line": 9,
      "unit_line": 9,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_two",
      "modals": [
        "recommended"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "Recommended practices are organized into two primary sections",
      "sha256": "ff66536141c3f6299deeb835e8929192b7fc2ea8db5ac4b082be314cc0fe68fe",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "16#1",
      "line": 16,
      "unit_line": 16,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "Feeds should be published at a public, permanent URL",
      "sha256": "c4fa1dc3ed2ce309dd91d88e03a063388577d48993427bf174065c1b200a0ede",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "17#1",
      "line": 17,
      "unit_line": 17,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "The URL should be directly accessible without requiring a login to access the feed.",
      "sha256": "7e316847fabe6ef0ca5458eaf566e3ad6e273f145adfd926ed9fe3c37de3cd2c",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "17#2",
      "line": 17,
      "unit_line": 17,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "If desired, API keys may be used but registration for API keys should be automated and available to all.",
      "sha256": "f1960559e5790a36d44b455518ffe6f074e00623e63946f9ea40d66abf70f754",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "18#1",
      "line": 18,
      "unit_line": 18,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "imperative",
      "found_by": "hand",
      "modals": [],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "Maintain persistent identifiers (id fields) within a GTFS Realtime feed (e.g., FeedEntity.id, VehicleDescriptor.id, CarriageDetails.id) across feed iterations.",
      "sha256": "3a57ca729f2c3137f8a47d22ee41720192fb742318746440d6540b7ad5daae46",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "19#1",
      "line": 19,
      "unit_line": 19,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "GTFS Realtime feeds should be refreshed at least once every 30 seconds, or whenever the information represented within the feed (position of a vehicle) changes, whichever is more frequent.",
      "sha256": "f47b16b27b77da41d732979753d20f7010743ef8a992e88e636c2fada5a17c7a",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "19#2",
      "line": 19,
      "unit_line": 19,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "VehiclePositions tend to change more frequently than other feed entities and should be updated as frequently as possible.",
      "sha256": "0b0f65783638cbe00e02fddd2474a820d73ac9743a712f3f0dd6e0921d913b0b",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "19#3",
      "line": 19,
      "unit_line": 19,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "If the content has not changed, the feed should be updated with a new `FeedHeader.timestamp` reflecting that the information is still relevant as of that timestamp.",
      "sha256": "89e5d2802761f748dea31259ca89e9beaaa81321993358730dd52868df1576ba",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "20#1",
      "line": 20,
      "unit_line": 20,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "Data within a GTFS Realtime feed should not be older than 90 seconds for Trip Updates and Vehicle Positions and not older than 10 minutes for Service Alerts.",
      "sha256": "b922b717d0ef82d4caaf17007df531a44ee08f69a53c27d6e0a629b5788eb032",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "20#2",
      "line": 20,
      "unit_line": 20,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "For example, even if a producer is continuously refreshing the `FeedHeader.timestamp` timestamp every 30 seconds, the age of VehiclePositions within that feed should not be older than 90 seconds.",
      "sha256": "352f371bb278bf754312225b930a22edad6e430eb7ca6cb0e0d321db7c6136cf",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "21#1",
      "line": 21,
      "unit_line": 21,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "The server hosting GTFS Realtime data should be reliable and consistently return validly-formatted protobuf-encoded responses.",
      "sha256": "d707b42e93ab92e235a347afb74d4834a1be1acd207f6f687146ef8c3545785a",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "21#2",
      "line": 21,
      "unit_line": 21,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "Fewer than 1% of responses should be invalid (protobuf errors or fetching errors).",
      "sha256": "5ba5b4886c1357f02d56c0541560a8a6d588f929861f0067c433a259e6e012ce",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "22#1",
      "line": 22,
      "unit_line": 22,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "The web-server hosting GTFS Realtime data should be configured to correctly report the file modification date (see HTTP/1.1 - Request for Comments 2616, under Section 14.29) so consumers can leverage the `If-Modified-Since` HTTP header.",
      "sha256": "90760a8d38dbf12e1f95b5127557701f6113f9a909a1fd93ce534896903fb200",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "23#1",
      "line": 23,
      "unit_line": 23,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "Feeds should provide protocol buffer-encoded feed content by default when queried via an HTTP request at the given URL - consumers should not need to define special HTTP accept headers to receive protocol-buffer encoded content.",
      "sha256": "653cb59253f267be0e6bab82f5b3f97a85a5e4bf0274672ebf3f6bfd9f0b48d5",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "24#1",
      "line": 24,
      "unit_line": 24,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "Due to how protocol buffers encode [optional values](https://developers.google.com/protocol-buffers/docs/proto#optional), before reading data from a GTFS Realtime feed consumers should check for the presence of values using the protocol buffer-generated `hasX()` methods before using that value and should only use the value if `hasX()` is true (where `X` is the name of the field).",
      "sha256": "02dd5fbf1e5a023a178eccfa37eea295b1e6af908d5d5dee843ef4b9a04d7032",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "24#2",
      "line": 24,
      "unit_line": 24,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "If `hasX()` returns `false`, the default value for that field defined in the `gtfs-realtime.proto` value should be assumed.",
      "sha256": "99029582ad3b60253ed519ee27ce274b3958704aed64297c640997d95314c4da",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "25#1",
      "line": 25,
      "unit_line": 25,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "Feeds should use HTTPS instead of HTTP (without encryption) to ensure feed integrity.",
      "sha256": "6f8da50764bba63c60bbfa3052fd4d9ba28382530c3732e538d642e9c78d4b09",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "26#1",
      "line": 26,
      "unit_line": 26,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "Feeds should cover the vast majority of trips included in the companion static GTFS dataset.",
      "sha256": "fc69543c725589cd22eade55460f468305511299f7fa6df69236c299011ce1fc",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "26#2",
      "line": 26,
      "unit_line": 26,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "In particular, it should include data for high-density and high-traffic city areas and busy routes.",
      "sha256": "71961eff30c8c836137a533d35cd040c2e91e71a091d3141839bf6dcaa0df236",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "34#1",
      "line": 34,
      "unit_line": 34,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "table_row",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "All GTFS Realtime feeds should be \"2.0\" or higher, as early version of GTFS Realtime did not require all fields needed to represent various transit situations adequately.",
      "sha256": "4c4e528bfb7b19872412939939c28f9bae292cafe7924befe55b475dfe172f06",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "35#1",
      "line": 35,
      "unit_line": 35,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "table_row",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "This timestamp should not decrease between two sequential feed iterations.",
      "sha256": "432e4deebf6317fa2f1f1b8155cf7aae70ca5534ce10a72dcfe4abb04a2efe85",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "36#1",
      "line": 36,
      "unit_line": 36,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "table_row",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "This timestamp value should always change if the feed contents change - the feed contents should not change without updating the header `timestamp`.",
      "sha256": "de5e3aeb0f704c59993121d6adfa0cab4daf760315245402040c869233b44f26",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "36#2",
      "line": 36,
      "unit_line": 36,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "table_row",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "*Possible solution* - Producers should provide a `Last-Modified` HTTP header, and consumers should pass their most recent `If-Modified-Since` HTTP header to avoid receiving stale data.",
      "sha256": "986cdaa784b24da93ec56cdb94ad79e2ce14547e5e3f7f60383d2c864609ea37",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "36#3",
      "line": 36,
      "unit_line": 36,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "table_row",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "cannot"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "ERROR"
      ],
      "text": "*Possible solution* - If HTTP headers cannot be used, options such as sticky sessions can be used to ensure that each consumer is routed to the same producer server.",
      "sha256": "73535bf25ad2eba316aa5227b5f0fa92fe18ebd18013dd284508e6c256cec1b2",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "40#1",
      "line": 40,
      "unit_line": 40,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "All entities should only be removed from a GTFS Realtime feed when they are no longer relevant to users.",
      "sha256": "9f7535b94e371ddf8f34fa04907b5d38472d8ffa0dd0f6e2ccc1246c07df8bc9",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "40#2",
      "line": 40,
      "unit_line": 40,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "If an entity is provided in one feed instance but dropped in a subsequent feed update, it should be assumed that there is no real-time information for that entity.",
      "sha256": "afc422d682eb95940ded261c82ae039f50ddc1a659707cab3730662b8e7ff6ff",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "44#1",
      "line": 44,
      "unit_line": 44,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "table_row",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "Should be kept stable over the entire trip duration",
      "sha256": "a9a6b8a9f589f4ecd5e22f8f5ed5c2b1b5955a38765fb9e181c7e083d81b49f8",
      "also_at": [
        114
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "50#1",
      "line": 50,
      "unit_line": 50,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "When canceling trips over a number of days, producers should provide TripUpdates referencing the given `trip_ids` and `start_dates` as `CANCELED` as well as an Alert with `NO_SERVICE` referencing the same `trip_ids` and `TimeRange` that can be shown to riders explaining the cancellation (e.g., detour).",
      "sha256": "592f0cdbcd1e8ed361667e0427308eac7aa2a7c6032efae9764ba3ef27dd700c",
      "also_at": [
        127
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "51#1",
      "line": 51,
      "unit_line": 51,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "If no stops in a trip will be visited, the trip should be `CANCELED` instead of having all `stop_time_updates` being marked as `SKIPPED`, unless the trip was a `NEW` or `DUPLICATED` trip and was subsequently canceled.",
      "sha256": "78b267b508f05fc5eed7b051e4e086d55d0617848814cbb635f190256546a672",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "56#1",
      "line": 56,
      "unit_line": 56,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "table_row",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "If separate `VehiclePosition` and `TripUpdate` feeds are provided, [TripDescriptor](#tripdescriptor) and [VehicleDescriptor](#vehicledescriptor) ID values pairing should match between the two feeds.",
      "sha256": "9044cbb1cceebec3eae75df2332715a3a84e3649a88ed6d389f29a1cc7a11e77",
      "also_at": [
        58,
        66,
        83
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "56#2",
      "line": 56,
      "unit_line": 56,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "table_row",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "For example, a `VehiclePosition` entity has `vehicle_id:A` and `trip_id:4`, then the corresponding `TripUpdate` entity should also have `vehicle_id:A` and `trip_id:4`.",
      "sha256": "2550b3f57967dbe99389f874c7a48982df3f7c5047a4879a1d7433bd5e2c3cdb",
      "also_at": [
        58,
        68,
        85
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "59#1",
      "line": 59,
      "unit_line": 59,
      "scope": "",
      "kind": "table_row",
      "found_by": "pass_one",
      "modals": [
        "should"
      ],
      "severities": [
        "WARNING"
      ],
      "text": "`stop_time_updates` for a given `trip_id` should be strictly ordered by increasing `stop_sequence` and no `stop_sequence` should be repeated.",
      "sha256": "503fff6202c07f6540b0d9d8455d0c059be690abe7656e035ea88a884e74db48",
      "also_at": []
    },
    {
      "id": "60#1",
